 The pages under `docs/` are this repository's source of truth for people and coding agents. This page says which page
 owns each fact; read it before writing one.
+
+## Kinds
+
+| Kind | Owns | Required content | Diátaxis type |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| [Philosophy](philosophy.md) | Standing trade-offs that guide future proposals. | One page with a lead and `Tenets`; each tenet rules something out and links decisions that apply it. | Explanation |
+| [Architecture](architecture.md) | The system's parts and how they connect. | One page with a lead, `Parts` and `How they connect`; link the reasons to their owning pages. | Explanation |
+| [Decisions](adrs/README.md) | Why a foundation decision was taken. | Numbered `NNNN-<slug>.md` records with a lead, `Context`, `Options`, `Decision` and `Consequences`; explain why each alternative lost and the choice won. | Explanation |
+| [Features](features/README.md) | Member-visible behavior. | A lead, the behavior and its reasons, and links to decisions that shaped it. | Explanation |
+| [Runbooks](runbooks/README.md) | How to respond to an operational trigger. | One page per trigger with a lead naming its owner, `Before you begin`, `Steps` with expected results, and `If it fails`. | How-to |
+
+A decision merits a record when reversing it changes more than one feature or module. A recurring trade-off belongs
+in philosophy; an implementation choice below that bar stays in the code and its review. Each directory's README
+lists its pages. Each fact has one owner; other pages link to it.
+
+The [glossary](glossary.md) owns shared terms and their rejected synonyms.
